1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,869
Good morning. I'm very pleased to have this opportunity to say a little about two exciting new developments in the city:

2
00:00:07,869 --> 00:00:09,040
the Brackenside Open-Air Swimming Pool

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,740
and the children's Adventure Playground in Central Park.

4
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:18,540
As many of you may know, the idea for these initiatives came from you, the public,

5
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:23,180
in the extensive consultation exercise which the City Council conducted last year.

6
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:27,020
And they have been realised using money from the SWRDC

7
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:29,900
the South West Regional Development Commission.

8
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,680
First of all, Brackenside Pool

9
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:35,139
As many of the older members of the audience will remember,

10
00:00:35,139 --> 00:00:40,051
there used to be a wonderful open-air pool on the sea front 30 years ago

11
00:00:40,051 --> 00:00:43,980
but it had to close when it was judged to be unsafe.

12
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:46,733
For the design of this new heated pool,

13
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:51,550
we were very happy to secure the talents of internationally renowned architect Ellen Wendon,

14
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:56,367
who has managed to combine a charming 1930s design, which fits in so well

15
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:59,380
with many of the other buildings in the area

16
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,216
with up-to-the-minute features such as a recycling system -

17
00:01:02,216 --> 00:01:05,500
the only one of its kind in the world

18
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,410
which enables seawater to be used in the pool.

19
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:13,140
Now, there has been quite a bit of discussion in the local press about

20
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:17,368
whether there would be enough room for the number of visitors we are hoping to attract,

21
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:21,250
but the design is deceptive and there have been rigorous checks about capacity.

22
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:24,080
Also, just in case you were wondering

23
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:27,463
we're on schedule for a June 15th opening date

24
00:01:27,463 --> 00:01:32,900
and well within budget: a testimony to the excellent work of local contractors Hickman's.

25
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:37,880
We hope that as many people as possible will be there on June 15th.

26
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:42,268
We have engaged award-winning actress Coral White to declare the pool open

27
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:46,290
and there'll be drinks and snacks available at the poolside.

28
00:01:46,290 --> 00:01:54,108
There'll also be a competition for the public to decide on the sculpture we plan to have at the entrance:

29
00:01:54,108 --> 00:01:59,190
you will decide which famous historical figure from the city we should have.

30
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:02,433
And now, moving on to the Central Park Playground,

31
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:07,118
which we're pleased to announce has just won the Douglas Award for safety:

32
00:02:07,118 --> 00:02:09,640
the news came through only last week.

33
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:14,196
The unique design is based on the concept of the Global Village,

34
00:02:14,196 --> 00:02:19,512
with the playground being divided into six areas showing different parts of the world -

35
00:02:19,512 --> 00:02:21,410
each with a representative feature.

36
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:23,940
For example, there is a section on Asia

37
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:28,884
and this is represented by rides and equipment in the shape of snakes,

38
00:02:28,884 --> 00:02:33,510
orang-utans, tigers and so on - fauna native to the forests of the region.

39
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:38,472
Moving south to the Antarctic - we couldn't run to an ice rink I'm afraid

40
00:02:38,472 --> 00:02:42,370
but opted instead for climbing blocks in the shape of mountains.

41
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:45,360
I thought they could have had slides for the glaciers

42
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,590
but the designers did want to avoid being too literal!

43
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:50,558
Then on to South America -

44
00:02:50,558 --> 00:02:53,240
and here the theme is El Dorado

45
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:57,250
games replicating the search for mines full of precious stones.

46
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,940
And then moving up to North America

47
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:05,048
here there was considerable debate - I know the contribution of cinema

48
00:03:05,048 --> 00:03:09,460
and jazz was considered but the designers finally opted for rockets

49
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:11,980
and the International Space Station.

50
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:18,287
Eastwards to Europe then, and perhaps the most traditional choice of all the areas:

51
00:03:18,287 --> 00:03:20,540
medieval castles and other fortifications.

52
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:22,220
Then last, but not least

53
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:26,830
moving south to Africa and a whole set of wonderful mosaics

54
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:31,940
and trails to represent the great rivers of this fascinating and varied continent.

55
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:37,260
Now, the opening date for our Global Playground is 10th July.

56
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:39,806
And again we'd love to see you there -

57
00:03:39,806 --> 00:03:43,080
so make a date and come and see this magnificent

58
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:46,170
original new amenity right in the heart of the city.
